e now online</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-03-07 - <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/blog/adms-version-09-now-available-joinup-consultation\">ADMS version 0.9 is now available on Joinup for consultation</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-03-05 - <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/blog/5-reasons-why-publishers-semantic-assets-should-consider-joining-federation\">5 reasons why publishers of semantic assets should consider joining the Federation</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-03-03 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/blog/gs1-europe-experiments-adms\">GS1 in Europe experiments with ADMS</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-03-03 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/blog/listpoint-will-join-european-federation-semantic-asset-repositories\">Listpoint will join the European Federation of Semantic Asset Repositories</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-02-23 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/us-datagov-includes-vocabulary-publication-service-its-platform\">US - Data.gov includes a Vocabulary publication service on its platform</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-02-19 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/blog/activities-adms-working-group-will-be-extended-one-month-it-will-now-close-26-march-2012\">Activities of the ADMS Working Group will be extended for one month. It will now close on 26 March 2012</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-02-09 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/blog/1200-reads-and-640-downloads-enthusiasm-around-adms-echoed-its-public-review\">1200 reads and 640 downloads - enthusiasm around ADMS echoed in its public review</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-02-07 - <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/blog/adms-public-review-has-officially-ended-6-february\">ADMS public review has officially ended on 6 February</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-01-24 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/blog/only-two-weeks-left-participate-review-asset-description-metadata-schema-adms\">Only two weeks left to participate in the review of the Asset Description Metadata Schema (ADMS)</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-01-06 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/eu-asset-description-metadata-schema-adms-open-public-review\">EU - The Asset Description Metadata Schema (ADMS) open for public review</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2011-12-14 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/adms-and-core-vocabularies-projects-are-now-available-joinup\">The ADMS and Core Vocabularies projects are now available on Joinup</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2011-11-22 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/new-draft-adms-specification-released-community-review\">New draft ADMS specification released for community review</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2011-10-07 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/towards-enhanced-federation-open-source-software-repositories\">Member State Working Group to continue ADMS specification</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2011-09-22 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/new-paper-published-towards-open-government-metadata\">New Paper Published: Towards Open Government Metadata</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2011-07-07 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/adms-case-study-publication-e-government-metadata\">ADMS: case study on the publication of e-Government metadata</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2011-05-18 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/federation-repositories\">Federation of Repositories</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2011-05-09 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/adms-community-publishes-first-draft\">ADMS: Community publishes first draft</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>\r\n	Related documents</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/node/55759\">adms-specification-v0.6</a></span></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<span style=\"font-size:12px;\"><a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/elibrary/document/adms-enabled-federation-semantic-asset-repositories-brochure\" style=\"font-size: 13px; text-decoration: none; \">ADMS-enabled federation of semantic asset repositories - Brochure</a></span></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/elibrary/document/adms-brochure\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">ADMS Brochure</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/cesar/document/cesar-virtual-meeting-2012-01-27-technical-aspects-federation\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">CESAR Virtual Meeting 2012-01-27 on the technical aspects of the federation</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/cesar/document/cesar-workshop-20120307\" style=\"font-size: 13px; text-decoration: none; \">CESAR Workshop 2012.03.07</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/cesar/document/digitalis%C3%A9rdk-will-join-first-wave-adms-enabled-federation\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">Digitalis&eacute;r.dk will join in the first wave of ADMS enabled federation</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/cesar/document/etsi-experimenting-adms\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">ETSI experimenting with ADMS</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/elibrary/document/federation-semantic-assets-repositories\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">Federation of Semantic Assets Repositories</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<div>\r\n			<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/adms/document/generate-adms-asset-descriptions-spreadsheet-refine-rdf\">Generate ADMS asset descriptions from a spreadsheet with Refine RDF</a></div>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<div>\r\n			<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/elibrary/document/good-practice-study\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">Good Practice Study</a></div>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<div>\r\n			<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/cesar/document/gs1-europe-experiments-adms\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">GS1 in Europe experiments with ADMS</a></div>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<div>\r\n			<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/elibrary/document/isa-deliverable-process-and-methodology-developing-core-vocabularies\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">ISA Deliverable: Process and Methodology for Developing Core Vocabularies</a></div>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<div>\r\n			<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/cesar/document/listpoint-will-join-adms-enabled-federation\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">Listpoint will join the ADMS-enabled federation</a></div>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<div>\r\n			<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/elibrary/document/proposed-adms-conceptual-model-and-controlled-vocabularies\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">Proposed ADMS Conceptual Model and Controlled Vocabularies</a></div>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<div>\r\n			<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/cesar/document/riha-will-join-first-wave-adms-enabled-federation\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">RIHA will join in the first wave of ADMS enabled federation</a></div>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<div>\r\n			<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/adms/document/skos-used-publish-controlled-vocabularies-defined-adms-web\">SKOS used to publish the controlled vocabularies defined in ADMS on the Web</a></div>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<div>\r\n			<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/8c/23/ab/ISA_Contributor_Agreement_v1.1.pdf\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">The ADMS contributor agreement</a></div>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<div>\r\n			<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/elibrary/document/asset-description-metadata-schema-case-study\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">The Asset Description Metadata Schema - Case Study</a></div>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<div>\r\n			<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/cesar/document/international-commission-civil-status-will-share-its-semantic-assets-using-\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">The International Commission on Civil Status will share its semantic assets using ADMS</a></div>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<div>\r\n			<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/category/licence/isa-open-metadata-licence-v11\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">The ISA Open Metadata Licence</a></div>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<div>\r\n			<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/elibrary/document/towards-open-government-metadata\" style=\"font-size: 13px; \">Towards Open Government Metadata</a></div>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n','<div>\r\n	<p>\r\n		&nbsp;</p>','',1462873423,2),(42444,507507,17365,'Core Location Vocabulary','<div>\r\n	The Core&nbsp;Location Vocabulary is a simplified, reusable and extensible data model that captures the fundamental characteristics of a location, represented as an address, a geographic name, or a geometry.</div>\r\n<div>\r\n	&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div>\r\n	<p><strong><em>The latest version of the Core Vocabularies can be downloaded from<br />\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_vocabularies/description\">https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_vocabularies/description</a>.<br />\r\n		(direct link to <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_vocabularies/asset_release/core-vocabularies-v11#download\">version 1.1</a>)</em></strong></p>\r\n	<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n	<h3>\r\n		Motivation</h3>\r\n	<p>E-Government Core Vocabularies are the starting point for developing interoperable e-Government systems as it allows mappings with existing data models. This guarantees Public Administrations to attain cross-border and cross-sector interoperability.&nbsp;&nbsp;Please refer to the&nbsp;<a href=\"http://joinup.ec.europa.eu/elibrary/document/egovernment-core-vocabularies\">eGovernment Core Vocabularies paper</a>&nbsp;on the approach and benefits of Core Concepts for further background.</p>\r\n	<h3>\r\n		Core Vocabularies Working Group</h3>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n	The&nbsp;Core&nbsp;Location Vocabulary&nbsp;is&nbsp;one of the three Core Vocabularies that have been developed in the context of&nbsp;<a href=\"http://ec.europa.eu/isa/actions/01-trusted-information-exchange/1-1action_en.htm\">Action 2.1</a>&nbsp;of the&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(207, 59, 0);\">(</span><a href=\"http://ec.europa.eu/isa/isa2/index_en.htm\" style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; line-height: 18px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(207, 59, 0);\">ISA&sup2;</span>) programme</a>.&nbsp;The specification is developed by a multi disciplinary&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-working-group-members\">Working Group</a>, with a total of 69 people from 22 countries, 18 EU and 4 non-EU countries (USA, South-Africa, Norway and Croatia), and several EU Institutions.</div>\r\n<div>\r\n	<h3>\r\n		Milestones</h3>\r\n</div>\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc\">\r\n	<li>\r\n		From November 2011 till February 2012&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_location/release/02\">version 0.2</a>&nbsp;was developed.</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		On 17 February 2012&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_location/release/02\">version 0.2</a>&nbsp;entered a month-long public review period, ending on 16 March 2012.</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		In March 2012 all comments of the public review period were discussed in a&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-working-group-members\">Working Group</a>&nbsp;meeting.</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		On 7 May 2012&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_location/release/100\">version 1.00</a>&nbsp;of the combined specification of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/description\">Core Business</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_location/description\">Core Location</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_person/description\">Core Person</a>&nbsp;Vocabulary was released.</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		On 23 May 2012,&nbsp;the Coordination Group of the&nbsp;<a href=\"http://ec.europa.eu/isa/\">Interoperability Solutions for European Public Administrations (ISA) Programme</a>&nbsp;has endorsed&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_location/release/100\">version 1.00</a>&nbsp;of&nbsp;the combined specification of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/description\">Core Business</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_location/description\">Core Location</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_person/description\">Core Person</a>&nbsp;Vocabulary.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>\r\n	Known implementations</h3>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://opencorporates.com/\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/sites/default/files/ckeditor_files/images/IHU_logo.png\" style=\"width: 180px; float: left; height: 40px; vertical-align: text-top\" /></a><strong><a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/news/core-business-and-core-location-vocabularies-piloted-greece\">Greek Tax Authorities business registry published as linked open data using core business and core location</a></strong><br />\r\n	<strong>Owner:&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"http://www.tech.ihu.edu.gr/\" target=\"_blank\">International Hellenic University</a><br />\r\n	<strong>Date:&nbsp;</strong>June 2012</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/node/63242\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"Report\" src=\"http://location.testproject.eu/BEL/Core_Location_Pilot-Interconnecting_Belgian_National_and_Regional_Address_Data.png\" style=\"border-bottom: rgb(0,175,240) 1px solid; border-left: rgb(0,175,240) 1px solid; width: 100px; float: left; height: 141px; border-top: rgb(0,175,240) 1px solid; margin-right: 10px; border-right: rgb(0,175,240) 1px solid\" /></a></p>\r\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/node/63242\">Core Location Pilot - Interconnecting Belgian Address Data</a></strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Participants:&nbsp;</strong><strong><a href=\"http://www.agiv.be/gis/organisatie/?artid=980\">AGIV</a>,&nbsp;</strong><strong><a href=\"http://www.cirb.irisnet.be/\">CIRB</a>,&nbsp;</strong><strong><a href=\"http://www.bpost.be/\">bpost</a>,&nbsp;</strong><strong><a href=\"http://www.fedict.belgium.be/en/\">FEDICT</a>,&nbsp;</strong><strong><a href=\"http://cartographie.wallonie.be/NewPortailCarto/index.jsp?page=GenActeursMET&amp;node=13\">SPW</a>,&nbsp;</strong><strong><a href=\"http://www.ngi.be/\">NGI /IGN</a>,&nbsp;</strong><strong><a href=\"http://inspire.jrc.ec.europa.eu/index.cfm/pageid/481\">EC INSPIRE team</a>,&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"http://ec.europa.eu/isa/\"><strong>ISA Programme</strong></a></p>\r\n<p><strong>Date:&nbsp;</strong>February 2013</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://www.geonovum.nl/content/huiskluis-open-samenwerken-met-linked-data\"><img alt=\"Home\" src=\"http://www.geonovum.nl/sites/default/files/geonovum_logo.png\" style=\"width: 150px; font-family: Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, \'DejaVu Sans\', sans-serif; height: 76px\" /></a>&nbsp;Geonuvum PILOD:&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"http://data.resc.info/bag\">HuisKluis - NetAge.nl Address &nbsp;Mapping of the Dutch &#39;Building and Address&#39; base register</a></strong><br />\r\n	<strong style=\"line-height: 1.5; font-size: 12px\">Participants</strong><span style=\"line-height: 1.5; font-size: 12px\">:&nbsp;Forum Standaardisatie, gemeente Amersfoort, gemeente Nijmegen, Hack de Overheid, Kadaster, Kwaliteitsinstituut Nederlandse Gemeenten, Ministerie van Infrastructuur en Milieu, InterProvinciaal Overleg, Geobusiness Nederland en Geonovum, Netage, ...</span><br />\r\n	<strong style=\"line-height: 1.5; font-size: 12px\">Date:</strong><span style=\"line-height: 1.5; font-size: 12px\"> June 2013</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3>\r\n	Related documents</h3>\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc\">\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/elibrary/document/isa-deliverable-process-and-methodology-developing-core-vocabularies\">ISA Deliverable: Process and Methodology for Developing Core Vocabularies</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/elibrary/document/core-vocabularies-case-study\">Core Vocabularies - Case Study</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"http://eGovernment Core Vocabularies\">eGovernment Core Vocabularies</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>\r\n	Related news</h3>\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc\">\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-09-19 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_location/news/should-base-registers-provide-http-uris-location-objects\">Should base registers provide HTTP URIs for location objects?</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-05-30 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/isa-member-state-representatives-endorse-key-specifications-e-government-interoperability\">ISA Member State representatives endorse key specifications for e-Government interoperability</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-05-22 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/blog/isa-presentation-about-enabling-data-interoperability-european-data-forum-2012\">ISA presentation about enabling data interoperability on the European Data Forum 2012</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-05-11 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/version-100-core-business-core-location-and-core-person-vocabulary-released-today\">Version 1.00 of the Core Business, Core Location and Core Person Vocabulary released today</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-04-06 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/w3c-gld-working-group-opens-first-public-working-drafts-comments\">W3C GLD Working Group opens first public working drafts for comments</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-03-27 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/key-specifications-interoperability-developed-eu%E2%80%99s-interoperability-solutions-european-public-a\">Key specifications for interoperability developed by the EU&rsquo;s Interoperability Solutions for European Public Administration (ISA) Programme to become W3C standards</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-02-17 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/eu-working-group-seeks-public-comments-e-government-core-vocabularies\">EU Working Group seeks public comments on e-Government Core Vocabularies</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2012-01-06 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/nl-base-registry-buildings-and-addresses-open-commercial-activity\">NL - Base Registry for Buildings and Addresses open to commercial activity</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2011-12-14 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/adms-and-core-vocabularies-projects-are-now-available-joinup\">The ADMS and Core Vocabularies projects are now available on Joinup</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2011-11-18 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/dg-markt-confirms-its-participation-core-vocabularies-working-group\">DG MARKT confirms its participation in the Core Vocabularies Working Group</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2011-10-12 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/isa-programme-pursuing-its-work-core-vocabularies\">The ISA Programme is pursuing its work on Core Vocabularies</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		2011-08-08 -&nbsp;<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/news/case-study-core-vocabularies\">Case study on Core Vocabularies</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>\r\n	Core Location Vocabulary Working Group</h3>\r\n<h4>\r\n	Information on collaboration</h4>\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc\">\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-working-group-members\"><strong>Core Vocabularies: Working Group</strong></a>&nbsp;: The current members of the Core Vocabularies Working Group</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"http://joinup.ec.europa.eu/mailman/listinfo/isa-cv-person-wg\"><strong>Public mail archive</strong></a>&nbsp;:&nbsp;the public mail archive of the mailing list of Core Location</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<strong><a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_location/document/core-location-collaborator-licence-agreement\">Core Location&nbsp;Contributor License Agreement</a></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>\r\n	Meeting minutes</h4>\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc\">\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-wg-virtual-meeting-20111121\">Core Vocabularies WG Virtual Meeting 2011.11.21</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-wg-virtual-meeting-20111201\">Core Vocabularies WG Virtual Meeting 2011.12.01</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-wg-virtual-meeting-20111207\">Core Vocabularies WG Virtual Meeting 2011.12.07</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-wg-virtual-meeting-20111208\">Core Vocabularies WG Virtual Meeting 2011.12.08</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-wg-virtual-meeting-20111215\">Core Vocabularies WG Virtual Meeting 2011.12.15</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-wg-virtual-meeting-20111222\">Core Vocabularies WG Virtual Meeting 2011.12.22</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-wg-virtual-meeting-20120105\">Core Vocabularies WG Virtual Meeting 2012.01.05</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-wg-virtual-meeting-20110112\">Core Vocabularies WG Virtual Meeting 2012.01.12</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-wg-virtual-meeting-20120119\">Core Vocabularies WG Virtual Meeting 2012.01.19</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-wg-virtual-meeting-20120326\">Core Vocabularies WG Virtual Meeting 2012.03.26</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_business/document/core-vocabularies-wg-virtual-meeting-20120327\">Core Vocabularies WG Virtual Meeting 2012.03.27</a></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_location/document/core-location-wg-virtual-meeting-20120403\">Core Location Vocabulary&nbsp;WG Virtual Meeting 2012.04.03</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n','<div>\r\n	The Core&nbsp;Location Vocabulary is a simplified, reusable and extensible data model that captures the fundamental characteristics of a location, represented as an address, a geographic name, or a geometry.</div>\r\n<div>\r\n	&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div>\r\n	<p><strong><em>The latest version of the Core Vocabularies can be downloaded from<br />\r\n		<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_vocabularies/description\">https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/core_vocabularies/description</a>.<br />\r','',1462891660,2),(151504,507749,56177,'ADMS-AP version 2.01 RDF Schema','','','',1463151242,2),(151613,507911,56177,'ADMS-AP version 2.01 docx','','','',1463669024,2),(151614,507912,56177,'ADMS-AP version 2.01','','','',1463669083,2),(151615,507913,56177,'ADMS-AP version 2.01 diagram','','','',1463669125,2),(150484,507914,56177,'ADMS-AP for Joinup version 2.0','<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>\r\n				<p>This page describes <strong>version 2.0 of the ADMS-AP</strong>, which is the latest release published.</p>\r\n				<p><br />\r\n					In December 2015, the ISA Programme of the European Commission launched an activity to revise ADMS-AP aiming to address requests for change coming from real-life implementation of the ADMS-AP.</p>\r\n				<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n				<p>For more information about the revision, please refer to:</p>\r\n				<ul>\r\n					<li>\r\n						ADMS Revision page:<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/adms_revsion/description\">https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/adms_revsion/description</a></li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						ADMS-AP revision issues: <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/adms_revsion/issue/all\">https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/adms_revsion/issue/all</a></li>\r\n				</ul>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:500px;\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>\r\n				<p><strong>Note</strong>: The ADMS-AP Importer of Joinup is not updated yet to import solutions described using ADMS-AP v2.0. Therefore, federated solutions need to be compliant with <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/adms/asset_release/adms-application-profile-joinup\">ADMS-AP v1.0</a> specifications.</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/adms/description\" style=\"line-height: 1.5; font-size: 12px\">Asset Description Metadata Schema</a><span style=\"line-height: 1.5; color: rgb(0,0,0); font-size: 12px\"> (ADMS) </span>specification was originally drafted to describe semantic interoperability solutions (previously referred to as semantic assets). This application profile of ADMS aims to extend the use of ADMS for the description of other types of interoperability solutions, meaning solutions covering the political, legal, organisational and technical interoperability layers defined by the <a href=\"http://ec.europa.eu/isa/documents/isa_annex_ii_eif_en.pdf\">European Interoperability Framework</a>.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The changes made from version 1.0 to 2.0 have been collected in an Annex, on the specifications. The alignment between DCAT and ADMS could be considered the main change of the new version, i.e. the use of DCAT classes instead of ADMS classes.</p>\r\n','<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>\r\n				<p>This page describes <strong>version 2.0 of the ADMS-AP</strong>, which is the latest release published.</p>\r\n				<p><br />\r\n					In December 2015, the ISA Programme of the European Commission launched an activity to revise ADMS-AP aiming to address requests for change coming from real-life implementation of the ADMS-AP.</p>\r\n				<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n				<p>For more information about the revision, please refer to:</p>','',1463669303,2),(150255,508315,56177,'CPSV-AP Revision WG Virtual Meeting 3','<p>This page provides the agenda and supporting information for the second meeting of the CPSV-AP Revision Working Group.</p>\r\n<h4 id=\"organisation\">\r\n	Organisation</h4>\r\n<p>Time: Tuesday 24 May 2016 from 10:00 to 12:00 CET (see this in <a href=\"http://www.timeanddate.com/worldclock/fixedtime.html?msg=CPSV-AP+Revision+Call&amp;iso=20160524T08&amp;p1=1440&amp;ah=2\">your time zone</a>)&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Web connection: <a href=\"http://ec-wacs.adobeconnect.com/cpsv_webinar3/\">http://ec-wacs.adobeconnect.com/cpsv_webinar3/</a></p>\r\n<p><strong>How to connect?</strong></p>\r\n<p>Please refer to the <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/adobe_connect_instructions_cpov.pdf\">Connection Manual</a> or to the summary below:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li>\r\n		Go to <strong><a href=\"http://ec-wacs.adobeconnect.com/cpsv_webinar3/\">http://ec-wacs.adobeconnect.com/cpsv_webinar3/</a></strong></li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		Click &lsquo;<strong>Enter as a guest</strong>&rsquo;, fill in your name and click &lsquo;Enter meeting&rsquo;</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		Click &lsquo;<strong>ok</strong>&rsquo; to agree with the Web Conferencing Disclaimer</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		Answer &lsquo;<strong>Start</strong>&rsquo; to the question: Would you like audio conferencing with this meeting?</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n		Choose how you would like to connect your audio (this option will only be available after the meeting host has arrived to the meeting):<br />\r\n		A)&nbsp;Choose &lsquo;<strong>Dial-out</strong>&rsquo; and insert &lsquo;your phone number&rsquo; to receive a call from the meeting;<br />\r\n		B) Choose dial-in to call the meeting yourself using a phone;<br />\r\n		C) Use a microphone.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>It is advised to use option A or C.&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Alternatively, if you would experience any problems, you can also manually dial in via</p>\r\n<p>Belgium: +3228081363<br />\r\n	France: +33182880967<br />\r\n	Germany: +498922061600<br />\r\n	Luxembourg: +35220880608<br />\r\n	United Kingdom: +442033189433<br />\r\n	MeetingOne Conference Room Number: 1323004<br />\r\n	<a href=\"http://www.meetingone.com/eu_eg/Access_Numbers\">Additional access numbers</a> are available.</p>\r\n<p>If you have never attended an Adobe Connect meeting before:</p>\r\n<p>Test your connection: <a href=\"http://ec-wacs.adobeconnect.com/common/help/en/support/meeting_test.htm\">http://ec-wacs.adobeconnect.com/common/help/en/support/meeting_test.htm</a></p>\r\n<p>Get a quick overview: <a href=\"http://www.adobe.com/products/adobeconnect.html\">http://www.adobe.com/products/adobeconnect.html</a></p>\r\n<h4 id=\"agenda\">\r\n	Agenda</h4>\r\n<table style=\"height: 13pt;\">\r\n	<thead>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th scope=\"col\" style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 34px;\">\r\n				Time</th>\r\n			<th scope=\"col\" style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 72px;\">\r\n				Owner</th>\r\n			<th scope=\"col\" style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 406px;\">\r\n				Subject</th>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</thead>\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 34px;\">\r\n				5&#39;</td>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 72px;\">\r\n				MAR</td>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 406px;\">\r\n				<p>Welcome and overview</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 34px;\">\r\n				15&#39;</td>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 72px;\">\r\n				PA</td>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 406px;\">\r\n				Applied changes&nbsp;to the CPSV-AP</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 34px;\">\r\n				85&#39;</td>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 72px;\">\r\n				PA</td>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 406px;\">\r\n				<p><a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/all\">Current issues</a>&nbsp;in the CPSV-AP</p>\r\n				<ol>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/changing-definition-public-service\">Definition of Public Service</a><br />\r\n						<br />\r\n						A Public Service is a mandatory or discretional set of acts performed, or able to be performed, by or on behalf of a public authority. Services may be for the benefit of an individual, a business, or other public authority, or groups of any of these. The capacity to act exists whether it is used or not, and the term &#39;benefit&#39; may apply in the sense of enabling the fulfillment of an obligation.</li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/event-assotiation-agent\">Event - assotiation with Agent</a><br />\r\n						<br />\r\n						proposal is to add a new class of Criterion (from CCCEV) to indicate the criteria that a user needs to satisfy to be able to use the service.</li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/addition-more-detail-role-agent\">Addition of more detail on the Role of an Agent</a> Proposes the addition of a new class of <em>Participation</em> linked to a class of <em>Role</em>. This is in line with the Italian model and W3C ORG Ontology (which is the basis of CPOV).</li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/updating-relation-between-business-event-and-public-service-class\">Updating the relation between the (Business) Event and Public Service class</a></li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/information-about-authentication-public-service\">Information about authentication for a Public Service</a></li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/additional-channels\">Additional channels</a> - Proposal is to drop sub class of channel and just have a controlled vocab of types.</li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/more-detail-period-time\">More detail for Period of Time</a> - Mostly schema.org but with twists</li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/extending-processing-time-property-public-service\">Extending the Processing Time property of a Public Service</a> Do we need to be able to distinguish between min, max and avg processing time?</li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/remove-has-creator-formal-framework-po\">Remove has creator from Formal Framework -&gt; PO</a> (Thomas D&#39;h)</li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/addition-properties-related-measuring-delivery-public-services-through-their-cha\">Addition of properties related to the measuring the delivery of Public Services through their Channels</a></li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/additional-properties-related-public-service-portfolio-management\">Additional properties related to Public Service Portfolio Management</a> Add status flag? (maybe) More? (propose not)</li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/need-cite-person-class\">Need to cite Person Class?</a></li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/contact-information/contact-point\">Contact Information / Contact Point</a></li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/indication-language-which-input-needs-be-provided\">Indication of the language in which an Input needs to be provided</a></li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/indication-whether-input-mandatory/optional-be-provided\">Indication whether an Input is mandatory/optional to be provided</a></li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/information-about-authentication-public-service\">Information about authentication for a Public Service</a></li>\r\n					<li>\r\n						<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/cpsv-ap/issue/subjects-public-service\">Subjects for Public Service</a> Is the CPSV has a property of sector - is that sufficient?</li>\r\n				</ol>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 34px;\">\r\n				5&#39;</td>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 72px;\">\r\n				MDK</td>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 406px;\">\r\n				Next steps</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 34px;\">\r\n				5&#39;</td>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 72px;\">\r\n				MAR</td>\r\n			<td style=\"line-height: 13pt; width: 406px;\">\r\n				<p>Q &amp; A and closure</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p id=\"materials\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h4 id=\"materials\">\r\n	Supporting materials</h4>\r\n<p>The meeting minutes will be published shortly after the meeting. Please share your comments via the public mailing list.</p>\r\n<p>The daigram below is the current version. This is likely to be removed after the meeting but is provided here as a handy talking point.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img alt=\"Class diagram for CPSV-AP\" src=\"http://philarcher.org/semic/20160512CPSV-AP.png\" /></p>\r\n<h4 id=\"docs\">\r\n	Additional documentation</h4>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/sites/default/files/adobe_connect_instructions_cpov.pdf\">Adobe Connect instructions&nbsp;</a></p>\r\n','<p>This page provides the agenda and supporting information for the second meeting of the CPSV-AP Revision Working Group.</p>\r\n<h4 id=\"organisation\">\r\n	Organisation</h4>\r\n<p>Time: Tuesday 24 May 2016 from 10:00 to 12:00 CET (see this in <a href=\"http://www.timeanddate.com/worldclock/fixedtime.html?msg=CPSV-AP+Revision+Call&amp;iso=20160524T08&amp;p1=1440&amp;ah=2\">your time zone</a>)&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Web connection: <a href=\"http://ec-wacs.adobeconnect.com/cpsv_webinar3/\">http://ec-wacs.adobeconnect.com/cpsv_webinar3/</a></p>\r\n<p><strong>How to connect?</strong></p>','',1464677770,2),(152066,508813,6363,'Joinup Open Source News Service - June 2016','<div style=\"border:1px solid #949494; background-color:#F5B00F; padding:5px; text-align: center;\">\r\n	<span style=\"color:#FFFFFF;\">If the newsletter is displayed incorrectly, click <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/newsletter/joinup-open-source-news-service-june-2016\" style=\"color:#FFFFFF;\">here</a> to view the online version.</span></div>\r\n<p>The OSOR Newsletter keeps you updated on Europe&#39;s public sector&#39;s use of free and open source software solutions.</p>\r\n<p>Have an enjoyable read &mdash; and visit us at <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/\">Open Source Observatory</a>!</p>\r\n<div id=\"editorial\" style=\"border-top: 3px solid #F5B00F; margin: 13px 0; padding: 16px 0;\">\r\n	<div class=\"outline-2\" id=\"outline-container-orgheadline1\">\r\n		<h2 id=\"orgheadline1\">\r\n			<em>A growing community</em></h2>\r\n		<div class=\"outline-text-2\" id=\"text-orgheadline1\">\r\n			<p><em>The number of public administrations using free and open source software is growing steadily, the European Commission&#39;s Open Source Observatory (OSOR) shows. Government organisation that use the software enjoy both lower cost and increased flexibility. </em></p>\r\n			<p><em>Last month, the former was illustrated by the <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/italian-military-save-26-29-million-euro-migrating-libreoffice?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Italian Ministry of Defence</a>, which expects to save EUR 26-29 million over the coming years by switching to the LibreOffice suite of office productivity tools. In May, OSOR reported that the second argument was <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu//community/osor/news/sweden%E2%80%99s-insurer-open-source-maximises-it-efficiency?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">the main motivation</a> for Sweden&rsquo;s Social Insurance Agency (F&ouml;rs&auml;kringskassan). &quot;Open source&rsquo;s inherent flexibility maximises IT value&quot;, OSOR quotes Mikael Norberg, CTO at F&ouml;rs&auml;kringskassan. </em></p>\r\n			<p><em>Both organisations are also typical examples of government organisations that take the next step. They realise they should reinforce the community of open source software developers, and they learn how to share their solutions with their public administration peers. </em></p>\r\n			<p><em>The Italian ministry will soon be publishing online the training material that it is using for the switch to LibreOffice, and this summer, the F&ouml;rs&auml;kringskassan will detail how it will share its code. &ldquo;We want to contribute to code development, we need to be part of the communities&rdquo;, Norberg told OSOR. </em></p>\r\n			<p><em>Both echo the words of the European Commission, when it announced the <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/european-commission-update-its-open-source-policy?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">update of its open source strategy</a> in December 2014: &quot;It is time that we contribute back.&quot; </em></p>\r\n			<p><em>Clearly, Europe is gradually gaining a community of public administrations that code together. </em></p>\r\n			<div id=\"survey\" style=\"border-top: 3px solid #F5B00F; margin: 13px 0; padding: 16px 0;\">\r\n				&nbsp;</div>\r\n		</div>\r\n		<div class=\"outline-2\" id=\"outline-container-orgheadline2\">\r\n			<h2 id=\"orgheadline2\">\r\n				Sharing &amp; Reuse Recommendations | <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/node/151756\">Have your say</a></h2>\r\n			<div class=\"outline-text-2\" id=\"text-orgheadline2\">\r\n				<p>The European Commission has <a href=\"https://ec.europa.eu/eusurvey/runner/Sharing_reuse\">opened for public comments</a> its ten recommendations to promote public administrations to share and reuse their ICT solutions.</p>\r\n				<p>Are these the right tips? Will these help encourage public administration take an active role in sharing and reusing software? The EC would love to hear back from you.</p>\r\n				<p>The deadline for submitting comments is 29 June. The results will available in July; publication of the final version of the recommendations is foreseen later this year.</p>\r\n				<p><a href=\"https://ec.europa.eu/eusurvey/runner/sharing_reuse\">Read More</a></p>\r\n				<div id=\"news\" style=\"border-top: 3px solid #F5B00F; margin: 13px 0; padding: 16px 0;\">\r\n					&nbsp;</div>\r\n			</div>\r\n			<div class=\"outline-2\" id=\"outline-container-orgheadline3\">\r\n				<h2 id=\"orgheadline3\">\r\n					Latest News | <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/newsandblog/all?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">View all news articles</a></h2>\r\n				<div class=\"outline-text-2\" id=\"text-orgheadline3\">\r\n					<table border=\"2\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" frame=\"void\" rules=\"none\">\r\n						<colgroup>\r\n							<col class=\"org-left\" />\r\n							<col class=\"org-left\" />\r\n						</colgroup>\r\n						<tbody>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<h2>\r\n										Italian military to save 26-29 million Euro by migrating to LibreOffice</h2>\r\n								</td>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<h2>\r\n										Sweden&rsquo;s insurer: open source maximises IT efficiency</h2>\r\n								</td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<strong>The Italian Ministry of Defence expects to save 26-29 million Euro over the coming years by using LibreOffice. </strong></td>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<strong>Open source&rsquo;s inherent flexibility maximises IT value, says Mikael Norberg, CTO at Sweden&rsquo;s Social Insurance Agency.</strong></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/italian-military-save-26-29-million-euro-migrating-libreoffice?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Read More</a></td>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu//community/osor/news/sweden%E2%80%99s-insurer-open-source-maximises-it-efficiency?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Read More</a></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n						</tbody>\r\n					</table>\r\n					<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" frame=\"void\" rules=\"none\">\r\n						<colgroup>\r\n							<col class=\"org-left\" />\r\n						</colgroup>\r\n						<tbody>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/majority-companies-galicia-use-open-source?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Majority of companies in Galicia use open source</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[Spain]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/estonian-town-koigi-latest-switch-delta?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Estonian town of Koigi latest to switch to Delta</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[Estonia]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/%E2%80%98open-source-values-match-municipal-public-services%E2%80%99\">&lsquo;Open source values match municipal public services&rsquo;</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[Europe]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/cambridge-contribute-cloud-computing?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Cambridge to contribute to cloud computing</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[United Kingdom]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/european-parliament-continues-promote-open-source?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">European Parliament continues to promote open source</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[Europe]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/all-eu-rd-articles-be-open-access-2020\">All EU R&amp;D Articles to be Open Access by 2020</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[Europe]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/study-sweden-should-boost-open-source-competence?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Study: Sweden should boost open source competence</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[Sweden]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/eu-standards-directive-needs-revision-researchers-say?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">EU Standards Directive needs revision, researchers say</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[Europe]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/open-source-governance-creating-prosperous-world-peace?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Open Source Governance: Creating a Prosperous World at Peace</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[General]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/hungary-increase-use-open-source-software?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Hungary to increase use of open source software</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[Hungary]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/german-experts-update-free-software-legal-review?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">German experts update free software legal review</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[Germany]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/france%E2%80%99s-rgi-v2-recommends-odf?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">France&rsquo;s RGI v2 recommends ODF</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[France]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/first-courses-online-italian-moodle-based-mooc?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">First courses online in Italian Moodle-based MOOC</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[Italy]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/european-space-agency-starts-6th-summer-code?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">European Space Agency starts 6th Summer of Code</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[Space]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/estonian-finance-ministry-seeks-oss-service-provider?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Estonian finance ministry seeks OSS service provider</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[Estonia]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n							<tr>\r\n								<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n									<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/news/european-unified-patent-court-goes-open-source?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">European Unified Patent Court goes Open Source</a> <span style=\"color: rgb(102, 102, 102); font-size: 13px;\">[Europe]</span></td>\r\n							</tr>\r\n						</tbody>\r\n					</table>\r\n					<div id=\"studies\" style=\"border-top: 3px solid #F5B00F; margin: 13px 0; padding: 16px 0;\">\r\n						&nbsp;</div>\r\n				</div>\r\n				<div class=\"outline-2\" id=\"outline-container-orgheadline4\">\r\n					<h2 id=\"orgheadline4\">\r\n						Solutions of the month | <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/og_page/solutions-month?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">View earlier &#39;solutions of the month&#39;</a></h2>\r\n					<div class=\"outline-text-2\" id=\"text-orgheadline4\">\r\n						<table border=\"2\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" frame=\"void\" rules=\"none\">\r\n							<colgroup>\r\n								<col class=\"org-left\" />\r\n								<col class=\"org-left\" />\r\n							</colgroup>\r\n							<tbody>\r\n								<tr>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										<h2>\r\n											Asterix parser</h2>\r\n									</td>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										<h2>\r\n											Signature Verification</h2>\r\n									</td>\r\n								</tr>\r\n								<tr>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										<strong>Reading and parsing of Eurocontrol ASTERIX protocol data from stdin.</strong></td>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										<strong>A web-based application for uploading of documents of various signature formats.</strong></td>\r\n								</tr>\r\n								<tr>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/software/asterix/description?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Read More</a></td>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/software/signature-verification/home?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Read More</a></td>\r\n								</tr>\r\n							</tbody>\r\n						</table>\r\n					</div>\r\n				</div>\r\n				<div class=\"outline-2\" id=\"outline-container-orgheadline5\">\r\n					<h2 id=\"orgheadline5\">\r\n						Latest software | <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/search/apachesolr_search/?filters=sm_facetbuilder_facet_node_type%3A%22facet_node_type%3Afacet_24%22%20tid%3A16106\">View all interoperability solutions</a></h2>\r\n					<div class=\"outline-text-2\" id=\"text-orgheadline5\">\r\n						<table border=\"2\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" frame=\"void\" rules=\"none\">\r\n							<colgroup>\r\n								<col class=\"org-left\" />\r\n								<col class=\"org-left\" />\r\n							</colgroup>\r\n							<tbody>\r\n								<tr>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										<b><a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/catalogue/asset_release/bube-source_code?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Bube</a></b></td>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										<b><a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/software/regenesees/asset_release/regenesees-181\">ReGenesees System</a></b></td>\r\n								</tr>\r\n								<tr>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										German implementation of LCP Directive, uses the EU Pollutant Release &amp; Transfer Register</td>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										R software for the analysis of complex sample surveys</td>\r\n								</tr>\r\n								<tr>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										<b><a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/software/eurotrace/asset_release/comext-standalone-v915\">Comext Standalone</a></b></td>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										<b><a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/asset/ocs/asset_release/ocs-18\">OCS</a></b></td>\r\n								</tr>\r\n								<tr>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										To store, analyse and retrieve statistical data</td>\r\n									<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n										For online data collection, in the context of European Citizens&#39; Initiatives</td>\r\n								</tr>\r\n							</tbody>\r\n						</table>\r\n						<div id=\"stats\" style=\"border-top: 3px solid #F5B00F; margin: 13px 0; padding: 16px 0;\">\r\n							&nbsp;</div>\r\n					</div>\r\n					<div class=\"outline-2\" id=\"outline-container-orgheadline6\">\r\n						<h2 id=\"orgheadline6\">\r\n							Latest Studies | <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/og_page/osor-case-studies?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">View all studies</a></h2>\r\n						<div class=\"outline-text-2\" id=\"text-orgheadline6\">\r\n							<table border=\"2\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" frame=\"void\" rules=\"none\">\r\n								<colgroup>\r\n									<col class=\"org-left\" />\r\n									<col class=\"org-left\" />\r\n								</colgroup>\r\n								<tbody>\r\n									<tr>\r\n										<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n											<h2>\r\n												Entrada, a Big Data platform for Internet domain name registries</h2>\r\n										</td>\r\n										<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n											<h2>\r\n												BIRD manages routing at world&#39;s largest Internet Exchanges</h2>\r\n										</td>\r\n									</tr>\r\n									<tr>\r\n										<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n											<strong>The R&amp;D team of the Dutch Internet domain name registry SIDN has recently made its Entrada platform available as open source.</strong></td>\r\n										<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n											<strong>The open source BIRD is used by the largest Internet Exchange Points in the world.</strong></td>\r\n									</tr>\r\n									<tr>\r\n										<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n											<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/case/entrada-big-data-platform-internet-domain-name-registries-available-open-source?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Read More</a></td>\r\n										<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n											<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/case/bird-manages-routing-worlds-largest-internet-exchanges?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Read More</a></td>\r\n									</tr>\r\n								</tbody>\r\n							</table>\r\n							<div id=\"events\" style=\"border-top: 3px solid #F5B00F; margin: 13px 0; padding: 16px 0;\">\r\n								&nbsp;</div>\r\n						</div>\r\n						<div class=\"outline-2\" id=\"outline-container-orgheadline7\">\r\n							<h2 id=\"orgheadline7\">\r\n								Upcoming Events | <a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/event/all?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">View all events</a></h2>\r\n							<div class=\"outline-text-2\" id=\"text-orgheadline7\">\r\n								<table border=\"2\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" frame=\"void\" rules=\"none\">\r\n									<colgroup>\r\n										<col class=\"org-left\" />\r\n										<col class=\"org-left\" />\r\n									</colgroup>\r\n									<tbody>\r\n										<tr>\r\n											<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n												<h2>\r\n													Open Source Circular Economy Days</h2>\r\n											</td>\r\n											<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n												<h2>\r\n													OpenSuse 2016</h2>\r\n											</td>\r\n										</tr>\r\n										<tr>\r\n											<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n												Experts, enthusiasts and innovators exchange ideas and solutions, prototype systems, products and designs for an open source circular economy</td>\r\n											<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n												The annual openSUSE community event</td>\r\n										</tr>\r\n										<tr>\r\n											<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n												09 - 13 June various cities across Europe</td>\r\n											<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n												22 - 26 June, N&uuml;rnberg, Germany</td>\r\n										</tr>\r\n										<tr>\r\n											<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n												<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/event/open-source-circular-economy-days?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Read More</a></td>\r\n											<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n												<a href=\"https://events.opensuse.org/conference/oSC16\">Read More</a></td>\r\n										</tr>\r\n									</tbody>\r\n								</table>\r\n								<table border=\"2\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" frame=\"hsides\" rules=\"groups\">\r\n									<colgroup>\r\n										<col class=\"org-left\" />\r\n										<col class=\"org-left\" />\r\n									</colgroup>\r\n									<tbody>\r\n										<tr>\r\n											<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n												<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/event/2016-open-source-conference-london?utm_source=newsletterJun16&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=link\">Open Source Conference London 2016</a></td>\r\n											<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n												06 July, London, UK</td>\r\n										</tr>\r\n										<tr>\r\n											<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n												<a href=\"https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/community/osor/event/typo3camp-berlin-2016\">Typo3Camp 2016</a></td>\r\n											<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n												08 - 10 July, Berlin, Germany</td>\r\n										</tr>\r\n										<tr>\r\n											<td class=\"org-left\">\r\n												<a href=\"https: